WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.223
Welcome. This is your ten-day plan for consonant blends.

2
00:00:03.673 --> 00:00:10.210
A blend is two letters side by side, and each one keeps its own sound. Here is one at the start of a word.

3
00:00:14.412 --> 00:00:15.422
The word is stop.

4
00:00:16.322 --> 00:00:25.078
The goal of this plan is a child who says every sound, even when two letters sit side by side, and reads blend words never seen before.

5
00:00:25.678 --> 00:00:31.366
That is the goal. It is not a promise. Day ten is a check, and it shows you where your child is.

6
00:00:32.166 --> 00:00:36.097
This plan is for a child who reads short words, like cat and hop.

7
00:00:36.547 --> 00:00:39.997
Often the child leaves a sound out, and reads stop as top.

8
00:00:40.447 --> 00:00:42.580
Or stops at words like frog and jump.

9
00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:49.822
It is a normal step. Said fast, two sounds side by side run together, so the ear catches only one.

10
00:00:50.272 --> 00:00:54.070
So this plan slows the eyes down. Every letter gets its sound.

11
00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:59.024
Here is what is inside. Ten days. One page a day, about ten minutes.

12
00:00:59.424 --> 00:01:04.569
Day one is a short check. It shows you where to start. Day ten shows you what changed.

13
00:01:05.019 --> 00:01:10.276
Every day has a short video like this one, for you. It shows you what to do before you do it.

14
00:01:10.876 --> 00:01:15.490
Day two starts with two sounds at the end of a word. They are the easiest to hear.

15
00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:19.097
Days three and four put two sounds at the start of a word.

16
00:01:19.547 --> 00:01:23.665
Day five is a halfway check. It tells you to go on, or to go back.

17
00:01:24.115 --> 00:01:28.053
Then more blends, words with five sounds, and on day nine a story.

18
00:01:28.503 --> 00:01:33.336
Some days will need a second try. Doing a page twice is not falling behind.

19
00:01:33.936 --> 00:01:38.281
When a word goes wrong, do not say the word. Say the same words, every time.

20
00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:41.618
Two letters, two sounds. Say each one. Then wait.

21
00:01:42.518 --> 00:01:49.005
Here is how each day works. First, watch that day's video. Scan the code on the page with your phone.

22
00:01:49.455 --> 00:01:55.368
Then read the yellow box at the top of the page. It gives you three short steps, with the words to say.

23
00:01:55.818 --> 00:01:58.966
Do the first job together. That takes about two minutes.

24
00:01:59.416 --> 00:02:03.734
Then your child carries on with the page, and reads three things to you at the end.

25
00:02:04.184 --> 00:02:09.029
On five of the days your child has a track to listen to. You press play and step away.

26
00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:14.956
You need the printed pages, a pencil, crayons, and scissors for the cards on day two.

27
00:02:15.406 --> 00:02:20.494
When you are ready, start with day one. It is a short check, and it takes about four minutes.
